IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-fixtures`
IMPORT `ucta-schedules`
IMPORT `ucta-p1-explanatory`

-- Tests for ucta-p1-explanatory.l4 (sections 11 to 14).  Every expected value is written from the text.
-- `mk dealing` takes: the party made the contract in the course of a business; the party held out as
-- doing so; the other party made it in the course of a business; kind of contract; goods of a type
-- ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption; the party is the buyer at auction or tender.

§ `s 12 - dealing as consumer`

-- s 12(1): (a) neither in the course of a business nor held out, (b) the other party is in business, (c) goods of a private type.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) fails: the party made the contract in the course of a business.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` TRUE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) fails: the party held itself out as making the contract in the course of a business.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE TRUE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) fails: the other party did not make the contract in the course of a business.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE FALSE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) applies only to a contract governed by the law of sale of goods or hire-purchase, or by section 7: a services contract needs only (a) and (b).
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `Another kind of contract` NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `Another kind of contract` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) fails: the goods are not of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A hire-purchase agreement` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) met for a hire-purchase agreement and for a section 7 contract.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A hire-purchase agreement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract, not of sale of goods or hire-purchase, under which possession or ownership of goods passes` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Whether the goods are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use is not given.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Where (a) fails, the unknown limb (c) does not matter: the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the party deals as consumer in relation to the other party` (`mk dealing` TRUE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 12(2): "on a sale by auction or by competitive tender the buyer is not in any circumstances to be regarded as dealing as consumer".
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the buyer is regarded as dealing as consumer` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a sale by auction or tender: subsection (2) is silent.
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the buyer is regarded as dealing as consumer` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Together: (2) overrides (1).
#ASSERT `s 12(1) and (2) the party deals as consumer` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) and (2) the party deals as consumer` (`mk dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) and (2) the party deals as consumer` (`mk dealing` TRUE FALSE TRUE `A contract of sale of goods` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 12(3): "it is for those claiming that a party does not deal as consumer to show that he does not".
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the party must show that a party does not deal as consumer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The party who claims to be a consumer: the subsection does not say what that party must show.
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the party must show that a party does not deal as consumer` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Subject to this": on a sale by auction or tender subsection (2) governs.
#ASSERT `s 12(3) the party must show that a party does not deal as consumer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 11 - the reasonableness test`

-- s 11(1): the court's judgment, given as an input, is the answer for a contract term.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- A notice is dealt with in subsection (3); a notice having contractual effect is in neither.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(1) the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that has contractual effect` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11(3): a notice (not being a notice having contractual effect).
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that has contractual effect` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) together.
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A contract term` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ss 11(1), 11(3) and 29(2) the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` `A notice that has contractual effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 11(2): for the purposes of section 6 or 7, regard is had to the Second Schedule's five matters.
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the matters to which regard is had in determining reasonableness under section 6 or 7` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`sch 2 the guidelines`)
-- For section 2, 3 or 4 the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the matters to which regard is had in determining reasonableness under section 6 or 7` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 11(2) second limb: "does not prevent the court ... from holding ... that a term ... is not a term of the contract".
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the subsection prevents the court or arbitrator from holding that the term is not a term of the contract` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the subsection prevents the court or arbitrator from holding that the term is not a term of the contract` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(2) the subsection prevents the court or arbitrator from holding that the term is not a term of the contract` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 11(4): where a person seeks to restrict liability to a specified sum and the question of reasonableness arises, regard is had to resources and insurance.
#ASSERT `s 11(4) regard is to be had in particular to the resources and insurance matters` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "Where" fails on either limb.
#ASSERT `s 11(4) regard is to be had in particular to the resources and insurance matters` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(4) regard is to be had in particular to the resources and insurance matters` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 11(4) the matters to which regard is had where liability is restricted to a specified sum` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (LIST `The resources the party could expect to be available to meet the liability`, `How far it was open to the party to cover itself by insurance`)
#ASSERT `s 11(4) the matters to which regard is had where liability is restricted to a specified sum` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 11(5): "It is for those claiming that a contract term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness to show that it does".
#ASSERT `s 11(5) the party must show that the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(5) the party must show that the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 13 - varieties of exemption clause`

-- s 13(1)(a), (b), (c): to the extent that this Part prevents the exclusion, it also prevents the variety.
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Makes the liability or its enforcement subject to restrictive or onerous conditions` (JUST TRUE) `Section 2(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts a right or remedy in respect of the liability, or subjects a person to prejudice for pursuing it` (JUST TRUE) `Section 3` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts rules of evidence or procedure` (JUST TRUE) `Section 4` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 13(1) last limb: "sections 2 and 5 to 7 also prevent excluding or restricting liability by reference to terms and notices which exclude or restrict the relevant obligation or duty".
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 2(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 2(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 5` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 6` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 7` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Sections 3 and 4 are not among "sections 2 and 5 to 7".
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 3` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts the relevant obligation or duty itself` (JUST TRUE) `Section 4` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "To the extent that this Part prevents": it does not, or that is not known.
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts rules of evidence or procedure` (JUST FALSE) `Section 2(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Excludes or restricts rules of evidence or procedure` NOTHING `Section 2(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An arbitration agreement and another variety are not among the varieties named in subsection (1).
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `An agreement in writing to submit present or future differences to arbitration` (JUST TRUE) `Section 2(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(1) the person can use the exemption clause to avoid the liability` `Another variety` (JUST TRUE) `Section 2(1)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 13(2): "an agreement in writing to submit present or future differences to arbitration is not to be treated under this Part as excluding or restricting any liability".
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the agreement is treated under this Part as excluding or restricting liability` `An agreement in writing to submit present or future differences to arbitration` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the agreement is treated under this Part as excluding or restricting liability` `An agreement in writing to submit present or future differences to arbitration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 13(2) the agreement is treated under this Part as excluding or restricting liability` `Another variety` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 14 - interpretation of this Part (and the other definitions the Act gives)`

-- The table: how each defined word is defined, and what the Act names.
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` business)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS Includes
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` business)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` goods)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `Has the same meaning as in another Act`
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` goods)'s `what it points at` EQUALS "Sale of Goods Act 1979"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `hire-purchase agreement`)'s `what it points at` EQUALS "Hire-Purchase Act 1969"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` negligence)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS `Has the meaning given by a section`
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` negligence)'s `what it points at` EQUALS "section 1(1)"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` notice)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS Includes
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` notice)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `personal injury`)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS Includes
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `personal injury`)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `competent authority`)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS Means
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `competent authority`)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` enactment)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS Means
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` enactment)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` statutory)'s `what it points at` EQUALS "conferred by an enactment"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `deals as consumer`)'s `section` EQUALS "s 12(1)"
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `deals as consumer`)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `in consumer use`)'s `section` EQUALS "s 5(2)(a)"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` guarantee)'s `section` EQUALS "s 5(2)(b)"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` `business liability`)'s `section` EQUALS "s 1(3)"
#ASSERT (`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` company)'s `how it is defined` EQUALS Means
#ASSERT count ((`s 14 and ss 1, 5, 12 and 29(3) what the Act says the word means` company)'s `what the Act names`) EQUALS 3

-- "business includes a profession and the activities of any Government department or local or public authority".
#ASSERT `s 14 the activity is within "business"` `A profession` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the activity is within "business"` `The activities of a Government department` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the activity is within "business"` `The activities of a local authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the activity is within "business"` `The activities of a public authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the activity is within "business"` `Another activity` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "personal injury includes any disease and any impairment of physical or mental condition".
#ASSERT `s 14 the harm is within "personal injury"` `A disease` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the harm is within "personal injury"` `An impairment of physical or mental condition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the harm is within "personal injury"` `A bodily injury` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14 the harm is within "personal injury"` Death EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14 the harm is within "personal injury"` `Damage to property or another loss` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "notice includes an announcement, whether or not in writing, and any other communication or pretended communication".
#ASSERT `s 14 the communication is within "notice"` `An announcement, in writing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the communication is within "notice"` `An announcement, not in writing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the communication is within "notice"` `Another communication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the communication is within "notice"` `A pretended communication` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the communication is within "notice"` `Something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "goods" and "hire-purchase agreement" have the meaning in another Act: the answer is that Act's, given as an input.
#ASSERT `s 14 the thing is "goods"` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the thing is "goods"` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 14 the thing is "goods"` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 14 the agreement is a "hire-purchase agreement"` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 14 the agreement is a "hire-purchase agreement"` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
